## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThis PR implements the new OpenXR spatial entities image tracking API. When supported by the XR runtime, this allows an XR device to use its cameras to detect an image that has been supplied to the runtime before hand.\r\nThe location and orientation of the image is then communicated to the application and virtual content can be anchored to the real world image.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe specification for this API can be found here: https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#XR_EXT_spatial_image_tracking\r\n\r\nI have a PR with an update demo implementation here: https://github.com/BastiaanOlij/spatial-entities-demo/tree/test_image_tracking\r\n\r\nTodos:\r\n- [ ] complete built-in tracking logic, currently rely on some logic in the demo\r\n- [ ] debug the discovery logic\r\n- [ ] update class reference","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123275/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123275/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}